# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2: React Router RSC (React Server Components) mode
# CSRF bypass. Both apps use client-side routing only (BrowserRouter/
# HashRouter, no server actions, no RSC) — this mode isn't reachable in
# either codebase. Fixed in react-router@8.3.0, which requires React
# >=19.2.7; upgrading is a separate, larger decision already deliberately
# deferred (both apps are pinned to React 18.2.0 — see ROADMAP.md's
# Phase 8/10 notes, pre-deletion, or git log). Revisit when that upgrade
# actually happens, not by silently ignoring this forever.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# CVE-2026-44705: tmp path traversal. Pulled in by @lhci/cli's legacy
# inquirer/external-editor/rimraf/chrome-launcher chain — @lhci/cli is
# already at its latest published release (0.15.1), which still resolves
# tmp@0.0.33/0.1.0; no newer upstream version exists yet to bump to, and
# there's no reasonable override target (tmp itself has no fixed release
# in either of its own 0.0.x/0.1.x lines per the advisory — 0.2.6 is a
# separate major with a different API). Dev/lint-time only (Lighthouse CI
# tooling), never shipped in either app's client bundle. Revisit when
# @lhci/cli releases a version with an updated dependency tree.
CVE-2026-44705
